memory-graphs/

# Loose memory entries. The two rules above protect LOCATIONS, not CONTENT: an
# entry moved out of the store (a scratch dir, a _to_delete/ folder, the repo
# root) instantly loses that protection and is one `git add .` from a public
# push — and an entry's FILENAME alone leaks names and topics. So also ignore
# the entry filename shape anywhere in the tree, plus the usual scratch dirs.
# No tracked file matches this shape; verify with:
#   git ls-files | grep -E '[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-.*\.md$'
**/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.md
_to_delete/
_scratch/
